---
export const prerender = false;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactForm from "../components/ContactForm";
---

<Layout
  title="Contact"
  description="Questions about garage probes, Arduino wiring, the dashboard, or building your own monitor? Get in touch—or explore the about guides first."
>
  <div class="page-shell page-stack">
    <div class="page-grid items-start">
      <div class="page-stack page-stack-relaxed">
        <section class="card animate-zoom-in">
          <h1 class="card-title">Get in touch</h1>
          <p class="card-subtitle">
            Building, debugging, or adapting garage monitoring? We read every message and reply as soon as we can.
          </p>
          <div class="grid gap-4 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Garage Temperature Monitor started as a practical build—Arduino probes in a workshop, JSON feeds on the
              network, and a dashboard to watch trends over time. If you are wiring your first DHT22, chasing a flaky
              reading, or sketching a similar project for your own space, this form is the fastest way to reach someone
              who has been through it.
            </p>
            <p>
              Tell us what you are working on. Useful details include your board and sensors, what the probes show
              versus what you expect, and links to any feeds or screenshots. Even a short note helps us point you in the
              right direction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="card animate-slide-up-fade">
          <h2 class="card-title">Good reasons to write</h2>
          <p class="card-subtitle">We especially welcome messages about:</p>
          <ul class="grid gap-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed [list-style:disc]">
            <li>Probe placement, averaging, or unexplained temperature swings</li>
            <li>Arduino firmware, wiring, or getting JSON feeds online</li>
            <li>Dashboard setup, history, CSV export, or account questions</li>
            <li>Feedback, feature ideas, or collaboration on the open-source repos</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card animate-slide-up-fade">
          <h2 class="card-title">Explore the guides first</h2>
          <p class="card-subtitle">Many answers are already documented—browse before you send if you prefer.</p>
          <div class="grid gap-4 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              The <a class="text-link" href="/about">about section</a> walks through the full stack: from
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/temperature-probes">temperature probes</a> and
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/temperature-changes">what causes readings to move</a>, through
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/arduino-sketches">Arduino sketches</a>,
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/arduino-circuit-wiring">circuit wiring</a>, and
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/python-feeds">Python relay feeds</a>, to the
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/data-flow">end-to-end data path</a> and
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/accounts-and-dashboard">dashboard tools</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              Try the <a class="text-link" href="/about/probe-demo">interactive probe demo</a> to see how sun load,
              doors, and outdoor temperature affect three zones—or read how this site is built with
              <a class="text-link" href="/about/astro-applications">Astro on Cloudflare</a>.
              When the guides do not cover your situation, use the form and we will follow up.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="btn-primary mt-6 inline-flex" href="/about">Browse all about guides</a>
        </section>
      </div>

      <ContactForm client:load />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
